  "section_notes": "S1 is fully safe: 24-hour reporting for all incidents, 72-hour customer notice, and explicit reporting before cause is known. S2 keeps the 55°C test and 5% permanent limit but delays it five years and allows corrective-action marketing, and gives customers numeric rates without public publication. S3 and S4 land in acceptable ranges with 6-year retrofit and 36-month suppression; S5 has a mandatory 8/100k recall with prompt notices but no serious-injury clause."
